<p><strong>Transcript:</strong> <em>We have all become accustomed to the convenience of online shopping, specifically the 'free returns' policy that allows us to order multiple sizes and send back what doesn't fit. However, what happens to those returned items—a process known in the industry as 'reverse logistics'—is actually a massive, hidden headache for retailers. You might assume a returned shirt simply goes back on the shelf, but the reality is far more complex and costly.
